# pyenv
#   For a library or app, you might want to share your .python-version.
#   You should decide if this file should be shared or not.
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
#   However, in case of collaboration, if delegates have different platforms or python versions,
#   pipenv may install different packages.
#   For a library, you should ignore Pipfile.lock.
# Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, poetry.lock should generally be tracked.
#   However, if you wish to ignore it, uncomment the line below.
# poetry.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, pdm.lock should generally be tracked.
# .pdm-python.map
# .pdm-build/

# PEP 582; used by e.g. pdm when local packages are installed
__pypackages__/

